   "page_count": 1,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "Reyes Flores and Barrera Clinic\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Nicole Taylor in consultation on June 08, 2025. Ms. Taylor presents with Type 2 diabetes, which was diagnosed on January 29, 2034, when she was 30 years old. The patient is currently 21 years old and has been managing her condition well with medication.\n\nOn the date of her visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 126/66 mmHg, and her weight was 184 pounds. Her recent A1c level was 9.7, measured on June 25, 2025. Her average A1c level over time is 9.5, indicating that her blood glucose control has been generally stable, though there is room for improvement.\n\nMs. Taylor is currently taking metformin 500 mg and sitagliptin 100 mg to manage her diabetes. There is no evidence of microalbuminuria, neuropathy, retinopathy, or coronary artery disease associated with her diabetes.\n\nIn addition to her diabetic management, Ms. Taylor has a history of tobacco use, having smoked half pack per day. She quit in May 2024. Unfortunately, she reports consuming approximately 41 alcoholic drinks per week. \n\nUpon physical examination, Nicole's vital signs were within normal limits, and there were no other acute findings during the examination. She reports no new complaints aside from her routine management of Type 2 diabetes.\n\n**Impression and Recommendations:**\n\nNicole Taylor’s Type 2 diabetes is currently well-controlled with her current regimen of metformin and sitagliptin. Given her A1c level of 9.7, I recommend reinforcing dietary and lifestyle modifications to help further stabilize her blood glucose levels. Continuous monitoring of her A1c and routine follow-up are essential. \n\nMs. Taylor should also be counseled on the importance of reducing her alcohol intake and maintaining abstinence from tobacco products. Regular physical activity, if not already part of her routine, should be encouraged to help manage her weight and overall health.\n\nI appreciate your collaboration in managing Ms. Taylor's care. Please feel free to reach out if there are any further questions or if additional information is required.\n\nBest regards,\n\nDr. Jacob Jackson \nEndocrinologist \nReyes Flores and Barrera Clinic\n"
    }
   ],
